T*(Cir. 1998\); Alger v. Ganick, O'Brien & Sarin, 35)Tj
T*(F. Supp.2d 148, 159 n.20 \(D. Mass. 1999\) \(citing)Tj
T*(Whitaker\); Blakemore v. Pekay, 895 F. Supp. 972,)Tj
T*(983-84 \(N.D. Ill. 1995\); Azar v. Hegay, 874 F.)Tj
T*(Supp. 1314, 1317 \(N.D. Fla.\), aff'd, 66 F.3d 342)Tj
T*(\(11th Cir. 1995\).)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  Mr. Adair is attempting to use an FDCPA claim to)Tj
T*(attack the existence of the underlying debt, a)Tj
T*(matter already determined definitively in the)Tj
T*(bankruptcy proceeding. "The purpose of the proof)Tj
T*(of claim is to alert the court, trustee, and)Tj
T*(other creditors, as well as the debtor, to claims)Tj
T*(against the estate." In re Fernstrom Storage &)Tj
T*(Van Co., 938 F.2d 731, 734 \(7th Cir. 1991\))Tj
T*(\(quotation marks omitted\). By allowing FMB's)Tj
T*(proof of claim, the bankruptcy court confirmed)Tj
T*(the existence of a debt for Mr. Adair. To succeed)Tj
T*(on the FDCPA claim that he has brought, Mr. Adair)Tj
T*(would have to show that the value of the)Tj
T*(Chevrolet is incorrect in the proof of claim; if)Tj
T*($19,841.43 is the proper value of the car, then)Tj
T*(Sherman & Sherman's claim is not fraudulent.)Tj
T*(However, Mr. Adair is foreclosed from)Tj
T*(collaterally attacking the valuation of the car.)Tj
T*(The amount of the debt is a matter already)Tj
T*(settled in another forum, the bankruptcy court.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  In sum, as Mr. Adair has framed his FDCPA claim,)Tj
T*(he contests the amount of the underlying debt,)Tj
T*(not the method employed by the defendants in its)Tj
T*(collection. The amount of the debt was determined)Tj
T*(definitively, however, in the earlier bankruptcy)Tj
T*(proceeding when a proof of claim was submitted)Tj
T*(prior to confirmation and Mr. Adair's bankruptcy)Tj
T*(claim was later confirmed. The amount of the debt)Tj
T*(therefore cannot be relitigated in a subsequent)Tj
T*(FDCPA action by operation of the doctrine of)Tj
T*(issue preclusion./10 )Tj
T*()Tj
T*(Conclusion)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(  For the foregoing reasons, the judgment of the)Tj
T*(district court is affirmed.)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(AFFIRMED)Tj
T*()Tj
T*()Tj
T*()Tj
T*(/1 Mr. Adair is now once again in bankruptcy)Tj
T*(proceedings. His return to bankruptcy does not)Tj
T*(foreclose this action because debtors in Chapter)Tj
T*(13 proceedings may bring actions in their own)Tj
T*(name to vindicate statutory rights. See Cable v.)Tj
T*(Ivy Tech State College, 200 F.3d 467, 472-73 \(7th)Tj
T*(Cir. 1999\).)Tj
T*()Tj
T*(/2 See Montana v. United States, 440 U.S. 147, 153)Tj
T*(\(1979\) \(setting forth the differences between the)Tj
T*(two related doctrines\).)Tj
ET

